---
// "We brought the agent. You bring what makes it yours."
// Two grouped halves of three cards each.
//   1. what it knows and can do: Tools, Knowledge, Skills (developer surface, primed by Hero code)
//   2. how it behaves for your users: Per-user controls, Schedules, Policies (multi-tenant surface)
// Followed by the configure → your-user-asks → they-get-back flow viz.
import YoursPillarDoodle from '../ui/YoursPillarDoodle.astro';
---

<section id="yours" class="section">
  <div class="container-x">
    <div class="mb-10 text-center">
      <div class="eyebrow">yours</div>
      <h2 id="yours-headline" class="h-section mx-auto mt-3 max-w-[760px]">
        We brought the agent. <span class="hl">You bring what makes it yours.</span>
      </h2>
      <p class="mx-auto mt-4 max-w-[640px] text-fg-2" style="font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.55;">
        Capable out of the box for general work. You bring what it knows and can do, plus how it behaves for each of your users.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Group 1: what the agent works with (developer surface, primed by Hero code) -->
    <div class="mx-auto mb-3 max-w-[1080px] text-center sm:text-left">
      <div class="eyebrow">what it knows and can do</div>
    </div>
    <div class="mx-auto mb-10 grid max-w-[1080px] grid-cols-1 gap-5 sm:grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-3 md:gap-6">
      <!-- Tools: key ring -->
      <article class="card p-7">
        <div class="mb-4">
          <YoursPillarDoodle kind="tools" />
        </div>
        <h3 id="yours-tools" class="font-medium text-fg-1" style="font-size: 18px; letter-spacing: -0.015em;">Tools.</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-fg-2" style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.55;">
          Your APIs, integrations, and custom functions, defined once. Whatever your backend can call, the agent can call too.
        </p>
      </article>

      <!-- Knowledge: stack of papers / folder -->
      <article class="card p-7">
        <div class="mb-4">
          <YoursPillarDoodle kind="knowledge" />
        </div>
        <h3 id="yours-knowledge" class="font-medium text-fg-1" style="font-size: 18px; letter-spacing: -0.015em;">Knowledge.</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-fg-2" style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.55;">
          What the agent should know before starting. Your docs, files, and workspace data, editable in the dashboard without a redeploy.
        </p>
      </article>

      <!-- Skills: runbook with folded corner -->
      <article class="card p-7">
        <div class="mb-4">
          <YoursPillarDoodle kind="skills" />
        </div>
        <h3 id="yours-skills" class="font-medium text-fg-1" style="font-size: 18px; letter-spacing: -0.015em;">Skills.</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-fg-2" style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.55;">
          How your team does the job, written once. The agent applies it across tasks, on top of your tools and knowledge.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>

    <!-- Group 2: how it shows up for your users (multi-tenant surface) -->
    <div class="mx-auto mb-3 max-w-[1080px] text-center sm:text-left">
      <div class="eyebrow">how it behaves for your users</div>
    </div>
    <div class="mx-auto mb-8 grid max-w-[1080px] grid-cols-1 gap-5 sm:grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-3 md:gap-6">
      <!-- Per-user controls: sliders -->
      <article class="card p-7">
        <div class="mb-4">
          <YoursPillarDoodle kind="controls" />
        </div>
        <h3 id="yours-controls" class="font-medium text-fg-1" style="font-size: 18px; letter-spacing: -0.015em;">Per-user controls.</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-fg-2" style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.55;">
          How much each of your users gets. Credits, runs, compute, models, tool access, all as config. You don't write a quota system.
        </p>
      </article>

      <!-- Schedules: calendar -->
      <article class="card p-7">
        <div class="mb-4">
          <YoursPillarDoodle kind="schedules" />
        </div>
        <h3 id="yours-schedules" class="font-medium text-fg-1" style="font-size: 18px; letter-spacing: -0.015em;">Schedules.</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-fg-2" style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.55;">
          When it runs on its own, per user or per workspace in your product. Weekly digests and Sunday-morning monitors as config, not a worker you maintain.
        </p>
      </article>

      <!-- Policies and scoping: fence -->
      <article class="card p-7">
        <div class="mb-4">
          <YoursPillarDoodle kind="policies" />
        </div>
        <h3 id="yours-policies" class="font-medium text-fg-1" style="font-size: 18px; letter-spacing: -0.015em;">Policies and scoping.</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-fg-2" style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.55;">
          What it can and can't do per user, per workspace, or per tier in your product. Set as scope, not `if` checks you'll forget to add.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>

    <div class="mx-auto max-w-[860px] rounded-[14px] bg-sunken p-8 sm:p-10">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 items-center gap-6 sm:grid-cols-[1fr_auto_1fr_auto_1fr] sm:gap-4">
        <div class="text-center">
          <div class="eyebrow">you configure</div>
          <p class="mt-2 font-medium text-fg-1" style="font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.4;">
            the pieces above
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="hidden sm:block" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg width="32" height="14" viewBox="0 0 32 14" fill="none" stroke="#111" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="opacity: 0.6;">
            <path d="M2 7 L 28 7"/>
            <path d="M22 2 L 30 7 L 22 12"/>
          </svg>
        </div>

        <div class="text-center">
          <div class="eyebrow">your user asks</div>
          <p class="mt-2 font-medium text-fg-1" style="font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.4;">
            for whatever they need
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="hidden sm:block" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg width="32" height="14" viewBox="0 0 32 14" fill="none" stroke="#111" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" style="opacity: 0.6;">
            <path d="M2 7 L 28 7"/>
            <path d="M22 2 L 30 7 L 22 12"/>
          </svg>
        </div>

        <div class="relative text-center">
          <div class="eyebrow">they get back</div>
          <p class="mt-2 font-medium text-fg-1" style="font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.4;">
            <span class="hl-soft">the work, done</span>
          </p>
          <!-- hand-drawn check annotation -->
          <svg class="absolute" style="top: -8px; right: -2px; transform: rotate(8deg);" width="36" height="28" viewBox="0 0 36 28" fill="none" stroke="#111" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M4 16 L 13 24 L 32 4"/>
          </svg>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="mx-auto mt-8 max-w-[760px] text-center font-medium text-fg-1" style="font-size: 19px; line-height: 1.5; text-wrap: pretty;">
      Same agent every time. Enough to ship <span class="hl-soft">an internal tool, a consumer app, or a feature buried inside the product you already have</span>.
    </p>

    <!-- Quiet footnote pointing at /agent. Matches Stack.astro's pattern: the
         marketing surface stays uncluttered, but the reader who's curious what
         the agent ships with has a deep-link to the elaboration page. -->
    <p
      class="mx-auto mt-10 text-center font-mono"
      style="font-size: 12px; color: var(--ms-fg-3); letter-spacing: 0.04em;"
    >
      curious what the agent ships with?
      <a
        href="/agent"
        style="color: var(--ms-fg-1); margin-left: 6px; text-decoration: underline; text-decoration-color: var(--ms-accent); text-decoration-thickness: 2px; text-underline-offset: 4px;"
      >see what's built in</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
